# The build context is uploaded to the Docker daemon in full before anything runs, so the two
# heavyweight directories below (~244 MB combined) are excluded first. node_modules is
# reinstalled inside the builder from the lockfile; data/ is a runtime volume and must never be
# baked into an image -- the database holds customer records.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
data

.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache

.git
.gitignore
.claude
.codex-tmp

# Secrets. .env.example is the only one that ships.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Source material and design notes, not needed to run the app.
Assets
Dataset
design-system
tests
*.md

# Analysis artifacts. `output/` is the bigger problem of the two: it collects exported
# workbooks (traffic_*.xlsx, model_dataset_export/) built from real lead records, and an image
# layer is world-readable to anyone who can pull it. Same rule as `data/` above -- customer
# data never gets baked in. `tmp/` is screenshots and scratch PDFs.
output
tmp
.backups

# ~24 MB of design comps and an Obsidian vault. Neither is read at runtime, and the build
# context is uploaded in full before the first instruction runs.
Redesign Reference
Vault
*.ipynb
.github
